From: Łukasz Buśko <lukasz.busko@guns4hire.cc>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: PCI: mediatek: add MT7988 with its PEXTP
 reference clock

The MT7988 PCIe hosts are described with the mediatek,mt7986-pcie
fallback, whose schema pins the host to exactly four clocks. Each MT7988
port drives its SerDes through a per-port transceiver PHY fed by the
topckgen pextp_p<n>_sel mux, so the MT7988 hosts need a fifth clock and
a compatible of their own to describe it.

Add mediatek,mt7988-pcie, paired with the mediatek,mt8192-pcie fallback
the driver already matches, and pin its clocks to the four infracfg
clocks plus pextp_clk.


Source: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25841
Source-commit: 81fcdc849ae8905e1b4ab4f43036de6d5e7576e8
Adapted-to: Linux 7.3

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/mediatek-pcie-gen3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/mediatek-pcie-gen3.yaml
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
           - enum:
               - mediatek,mt7981-pcie
               - mediatek,mt7986-pcie
+              - mediatek,mt7988-pcie
               - mediatek,mt8188-pcie
               - mediatek,mt8189-pcie
               - mediatek,mt8195-pcie
@@ -272,6 +273,36 @@
             - const: tl_26m
             - const: peri_26m
             - const: top_133m
+
+        resets:
+          minItems: 1
+          maxItems: 2
+
+        reset-names:
+          minItems: 1
+          maxItems: 2
+
+        mediatek,pbus-csr: false
+
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            enum:
+              - mediatek,mt7988-pcie
+    then:
+      properties:
+        clocks:
+          minItems: 5
+          maxItems: 5
+
+        clock-names:
+          items:
+            - const: pl_250m
+            - const: tl_26m
+            - const: peri_26m
+            - const: top_133m
+            - const: pextp_clk
 
         resets:
           minItems: 1
